From 3f7600ded0d98902ec689543fa29ad4fdc0d3e6e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: worker <worker@baseharbor.local>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 01:02:50 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] fix(0428-142 r2): emit real unreachable backend-witness from
 resolved signal (CODEX-REVIEW r2)

Befund 1 (content): the per-backend witness derived every state from
manifest flags; 'unreachable' was declared (app_status_result.go:64-65) but
never emitted. Derive each backend's state from a real resolved backend
signal instead of a manifest flag:
  - Prometheus from ResolveHostDashboardSignalStatus (declared AND resolved
    supported => configured; declared but not resolved => unreachable;
    signal absent => not-configured)
  - Loki/Tempo from their own PersesBackendSignalWitness provenance
  Same change wired through both faces (app_status_result.go +
  perses_lifecycle.go); the two faces never drift.
  - Test helper gains configureTestTarget(t) env setup so the witness path
    resolves; rewrite the witness tests and add a test asserting
    'unreachable' against a declared-but-unresolved backend signal (not a
    flag), plus a reason-witness.

Befund 2 (records): correct the false 'validate => success' claim in
fix-2.md:35/105/124 to the witnessed API state (run API: validate=skipped,
optional owner-draht 114(a) cell); required aggregate PR Selected Checks is
the pass.

Befund 3 (knowledge, not a fix): after merging #1702 to develop 40cb28c the
four CLI shards stay red (0428-204); this PR touches nothing in
cmd/baha/main.go, internal/operatorauth/** or 0428-204 tests.

Scope: exactly the PR witness files (cmd/baha/app_status_result.go,
cmd/baha/app_status_result_test.go, cmd/baha/perses_lifecycle.go). No
subagent; self-run.
